<h2>Your account and privacy</h2>
<p>This page describes how account, payment and conversation information is used by {BRAND.name}. Only provide information needed for the feature you choose to use.</p>
<h2>Privacy questions</h2>
<p>For privacy questions or data requests, contact <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.emails.support}`}>{BRAND.emails.support}</a>. You can also use the <a href="/grievance">grievance process</a>.</p>
<h2>Information needed for the service</h2>
<ul><li>Account and phone-verification details to identify users and connect calls; age and disclaimer acceptance timestamps.</li><li>Call participants, connection and end times, outcome, rate and billing for service delivery, settlement, and safety review.</li><li>A recording of every call, the text made from it, and the result of our safety check (see <em>Call recordings and safety checks</em> below).</li><li>Strikes, appeals and decisions about an account.</li><li>Payment and wallet entries, influencer earnings, reports, influencer blocks and private caller tags, and complaint review records.</li><li>Service WhatsApp messages and replies used for call summaries, blocking, reporting, and caller tags.</li><li>Your voice introduction (if you are an influencer): public on your profile once approved; deleted when you close your influencer account.</li></ul>
<h2>Number masking and privacy on calls</h2>
<p>Nobody listens to calls live. Every call is recorded for safety; see <em>Call recordings and safety checks</em> below and the <a href="/safety">safety centre</a>.</p>
<p>Calls are designed to show a service number instead of the other participant's phone number. Masking does not hide numbers from the service or its telephony provider. Do not share personal contact details during a call.</p>
<h2>Call recordings and safety checks</h2>
<p>Every call is recorded for safety. The recording is kept in private storage, never on a public page. After the call, an AI system turns it into text (Hindi, Hinglish and other languages) and checks the text against our <a href="/community-guidelines">community guidelines</a>. Women-only calls are recorded and checked in the same way. We use this only to keep people safe and to decide strikes and appeals. We never sell it and never use it for advertising.</p>
<p><strong>Who can read it.</strong> Only named members of our safety team can read the text of a call. They first see only the flagged line and two lines before and after it. To open the full text they must type a reason, and every opening is logged. A strike message shows you only your own words, never the other person's.</p>
<p><strong>How long we keep it.</strong></p>
<ul><li>Recording, when the check finds nothing: deleted right after it is turned into text.</li><li>Recording, when the check flags a problem or a fan or influencer reports the call: 30 days.</li><li>Text of the call: 30 days if nothing was found, 1 year if it was flagged.</li><li>Check results, strikes, appeals and decisions: 1 year.</li></ul>
<p>Records needed for a dispute, payments or a lawful request may be kept for the period the law needs.</p>
<h2>Providers and access</h2>
<p>Service providers process information needed for authentication, telephony, WhatsApp delivery and payments. Clerk provides account login. Payment details are shown before a purchase. Gemini (Google) transcribes an influencer’s voice introduction for safety checks. Access to call details and reports is restricted to authorised service and safety functions.</p>
<h2>Retention and requests</h2>
<p>We keep call details (time, length, price, how the call ended) for 1 year, in line with the DPDP Rules 2025, which ask us to keep records for at least one year. Records needed for payments, disputes or lawful requests may be retained for the applicable period.</p>
<p>You may request access, correction, deletion, or a review after identity verification. The <a href="/data-deletion">deletion page</a> explains the process and its limits. This service is intended only for adults aged 18 or older.</p>
<h2>Data protection law we follow</h2>
<p>{BRAND.name} follows India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023 and the DPDP Rules, 2025. We never sell your data and never use it for advertising.</p>
<h2>What we collect from callers</h2>
<ul>
<li>Your WhatsApp number, checked with a one-time code.</li>
<li>The phone number you receive calls on. It can be the same number.</li>
<li>Wallet top-ups made by UPI.</li>
<li>Call details: time, length, price and how the call ended.</li>
</ul>
<p>Influencers never see your phone number.</p>
<h2>What we collect from influencers</h2>
<p>Influencers provide a WhatsApp number, withdrawal details (your UPI ID), and a voice introduction that they record themselves. Your voice introduction is public on your profile once our team approves it, and it is deleted when you close your influencer account. Gemini (Google) transcribes introductions so we can check them for phone numbers and other contact details.</p>
<h2>Avatars and AI content</h2>
<p>To protect influencer privacy, each influencer chooses an avatar. The photos on an influencer profile are AI-generated from that avatar and are labelled as AI. The voice introduction on an influencer profile is the influencer’s own recording, labelled “Recorded by the influencer”. The person you talk to is a real influencer.</p>
<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
<p>We keep influencer account data while the person is an influencer and for 1 year after, unless another law requires longer. Call details are kept as described in the retention section below.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can see your data, correct it, delete it, withdraw your consent, and nominate someone to act for you. Use the <a href="/data-deletion">deletion page</a> or write to our <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.emails.grievance}`}>grievance contact</a>. We reply within the time the law allows, which is 90 days at most.</p>
<h2>Data breaches</h2>
<p>If a data breach affects you, we will tell you and the Data Protection Board of India, as the law requires.</p>
<h2>Grievance contact</h2>
<p>To complain about how we handle your data, contact our <a href="/grievance">grievance contact</a> at <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.emails.grievance}`}>{BRAND.emails.grievance}</a>. If you are not satisfied, you can approach the Data Protection Board of India.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
